<article class="env-definition" id="06BN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06BN">Definition <span data-tag="06BN">76.44.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $i : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say $i$ is a <em>Koszul-regular immersion</em> if $i$ is representable and the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/06BM" data-tag="06BM">76.44.1</a> hold with $\mathcal{P}(f) =$“$f$ is a Koszul-regular immersion”. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $i$ is an <em>$H_1$-regular immersion</em> if $i$ is representable and the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/06BM" data-tag="06BM">76.44.1</a> hold with $\mathcal{P}(f) =$“$f$ is an $H_1$-regular immersion”. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $i$ is a <em>quasi-regular immersion</em> if $i$ is representable and the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/06BM" data-tag="06BM">76.44.1</a> hold with $\mathcal{P}(f) =$“$f$ is a quasi-regular immersion”. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>